 ................   T H E M E   O F   T H E   M O N T H ...............
                       HIGH PERFORMANCE COMPUTING

 A previous edition of DECNEWS covered workstation farms and their role
 in Scientific and Technical computing. This edition provides a brief
 overview of technical computing and introduces the new Digital 2100
 affordable multiprocessor compute server.

 SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL COMPUTING WITH ALPHA AXP........Technical
 computing is the ability to solve business and scientific problems
 through the use of computer modeling, simulation, and analysis. With
 Alpha AXP, technical or high performance computing is being used to
 model financial dynamics, visualize database information, design
 consumer products, and evaluate manufacturing processes. It has been
 used successfully in the fields of Computational Chemistry, Molecular
 Science/Simulation, Mechanical Computer-Aided Design, and Computational
 Fluid Dynamics.

 Technical computing requires performance -- the raw speed to do big
 jobs quickly! The best way to get performance is with a single fast
 processor. Alpha AXP based systems have emerged as the leader in
 technical computing because of their exceptional performance. Although
 performance limits are being continually exceeded with new generations
 of Alpha AXP processors being developed, there are limits on how fast a
 single processor can be. The way to improve performance is to use
 several processors in parallel. There are many ways to build parallel
 systems depending on your performance needs. Alpha AXP processors today
 can execute several instructions at the same time, and future gener-
 ations will be able to execute many more instructions simultaneously.

 ALTERNATIVES FOR PARALLEL SYSTEMS.......In choosing a parallel system,
 you need to consider required performance and the characteristics of
 the application. If the application can be broken apart into large
 pieces that do not need to communicate with each other very much, a
 workstation cluster, such as the AdvantageCluster family, is an
 excellent choice. In a workstation cluster (or "distributed memory"
 system), each processor has its own memory, I/O, and communications.
 These workstation clusters can be scaled to dozens or even hundreds of
 processors, can easily be added to, and support the latest generations
 of hardware. They are an excellent choice for both large batch work-
 loads as well as parallel processing.

 Many applications can only be broken into small pieces that require
 extensive interaction and communication. This may be due to the
 algorithms used in the application, or to the way the application has
 been written. In this case a shared memory multi-processor such as the
 Digital 2100 or DEC 7000 is an excellent choice. The processors can
 communicate with each other and share information using the high
 performance shared memory. Shared memory multiprocessors have hard
 limits on the number of processors they support, and typically require
 all of the processors be identical. These systems can be combined into
 "workstation clusters" -- either a cluster made entirely of multi-
 processors or as high performance compute nodes in a configuration
 including workstations.

 ANNOUNCING THE DIGITAL 2100 SERVER A500MP........Digital recently
 announced the Digital 2100 Server A500MP, a high performance Alpha AXP
 symmetric multiprocessing (SMP) PCI/EISA based server. The server is
 expandable from one to four processors and offers support for DEC
 OSF/1, OpenVMS AXP, and Windows NT. It functions as a high-availability
 application server for process control and point-of-sale systems, a
 high-capacity database server for financial and medical markets, a
 PC-LAN superserver, or a cost-effective alternative for mainframe
 downsizing. The system comes with worldwide, three-year, 24-hour
 response, on-site warranty. Best of all, the Digital 2100 Server is
 amazingly affordable. Due to the high-value design and manufacturing
 philosopy used, Digital is able to offer the new server at an industry
 leading price.

 * Fact Sheet - Digital 2100 Server Model A500MP; news0501.txt

 DIGITAL HIGH PERFORMANCE COMPUTING EXPERTISE CENTERS PROVIDE TECHNICAL
 CONSULTING WORLDWIDE........Digital's High Performance Computing (HPC)
 Expertise Centers bring together highly qualified individuals and
 extensive hardware and software technologies so customers can learn how
 to get the most out of their investments in Alpha AXP workstations,
 Alpha AXP farms, SMP systems, servers, and other high performance
 products. Digital has expanded its commitment to the HPC Expertise
 Centers, serving customers worldwide through eleven centers around the
 globe. HPC Expertise Centers provide tailored customer visits, bench-
 marks, demonstrations, application optimization, consulting services
 and collateral materials. To learn more about how the HPC worldwide
 network of Expertise Centers can meet your needs, please contact your
 local sales representative or Authorized Reseller.

 ..................... A N N O U N C E M E N T S ......................

 INTERNET SECURITY SERVICES ANNOUNCED........Digital has announced the
 availability of Internet Security Services, customized consulting
 services to help clients ensure a high level of security between their
 private networks and the Internet global network and other public
 networks. The premier component of these services is SEAL (Screening
 External Access Link), a combination of expert security consulting and
 software capabilities that delivers a protected and programmable
 "firewall" through a screened intelligent gateway to guard private
 networks while enabling users to have controlled links to Internet and
 other networks. These services can also be used to protect sensitive
 areas of internal networks. Internet Security Services are available
 immediately in the United States, Canada, Latin America and Europe, and
 will be available in Asia later this calendar year.

 * Fact Sheet and Q&A on Internet Security Services; news0503.txt
 * Press Release on Internet Security Services (U.S.); news0504.txt
 * Press Release on Internet Security Services (Europe); news0505.txt

 CHANNELWORKS AVAILABLE WORLDWIDE.......Digital's ChannelWorks product,
 a unique bridge allowing computer systems to extend data networks over
 existing cable television wiring, is now available worldwide. With the
 ChannelWorks bridge, broadband ethernet local area network capabilities
 are available over existing TV channels to any equipped sites across
 the community on the cable TV network, providing high-speed data
 communications. It is particularly useful for institutions that use
 videoconferencing or must share data-intensive applications such as
 graphics and mapping. The first installation of ChannelWorks in Europe
 is at the University of Wageningen in Holland, which was featured in
 the April issue of DECNEWS.

 DIGITAL EXPANDS STRATEGIC ALLIANCE WITH STERN COMPUTING SYSTEMS......
 Stern Computing Systems recently announced its SSP (Shared Sustained
 Performance) product range incorporating its own SSP/RISC architecture
 and SSP/SOFT software technologies. SSP/Application nodes, featuring
 Digital's AlphaGeneration server hardware is immediately availability
 through a newly expanded strategic alliance with Digital Equipment
 Corporation. SSP/Application nodes focus on industrial markets for
 high-performance computers by running existing unmodified software at
 supercomputer speeds. With Stern's SSP/SOFT, the full range of Alpha-
 Generation servers can immediately be used to solve technical and
 scientific problems at workstation price/performance levels.

 GARTNER GROUP SURVEY SCORES DIGITAL HIGH IN ISV COMPUTATIONAL CHEMISTRY
 SOFTWARE AVAILABILITY........A recent Gartner Group survey targeted
 computational chemistry ISV's, who were asked about the availability of
 their software on a range of Massively Parallel, SMP, and Workstation
 Farm high performance computing platforms. Results indicated that
 Digital scored the second highest in ISV computational chemistry
 software availability and commitment. "Vendors whose workstations have
 achieved broad penetration of the chemistry and pharmaceutical markets
 have also achieved the broadest success in getting ISV's to port
 applications to their platforms".

 NEW PARALLEL COMPUTATIONAL CHEMISTRY WORKSTATION FARM PORT "AMBER"....A
 parallelized PVM-based Workstation Farm version of AMBER 4.0 is now
 available for Alpha AXP OSF/1 Workstation Farms. AMBER is a computa-
 tional chemistry application used extensively by pharmaceutical
 chemists. The developers will provide the code free via FTP or for $50
 by tape to customers that are already licensed for the single cpu
 versions of AMBER 4.0.

