 OXFORD UNIVERSITY IS FIRST U.K. CUSTOMER TO PURCHASE DIGITAL'S NEW
 DIGITAL 2100 SERVER......Oxford University recently purchased Digital's
 new symmetric multiprocessing Alpha AXP server, the Digital 2100 Server
 Model A500MP, for their Computer Services department. Alex Reid,
 Director of Computer Services at Oxford University, said "We purchased
 the server to handle increased demand for computing power, and will use
 it as a general computing resource for students and staff right across
 the University." The server will run OSF/1 and will be accessed by up
 to 200 users at any one time throughout the university's departments
 and colleges. It will accommodate up to four Alpha AXP processors using
 symmetric multiprocessing techniques, so that cost-effective and swift
 upgrades can be achieved. The university indicated that the Alpha AXP
 64-bit architecture was a crucial factor in the decision to purchase
 the Digital 2100 Server over the Sun SparcServer.

 * Contact: Alex Reid, Director of Oxford University Computing Services,
   alex.reid@oucs.ox.ac.uk

