 TO COPY SUPPORTING DOCUMENTS:

 Readers may obtain additional information about DECNEWS items by
 requesting full texts of supporting documents, which are marked with an
 asterisk at the end of each item.

 Supporting documents referenced in DECNEWS can be copied electronically
 by anonymous file transfer protocol (FTP) on the Digital public access
 gateway (see instructions below), or by sending a GET filename command
 (e.g. GET news0110 txt) to LISTSERV@UBVM.BITNET or
 LISTSERV@UBVM.CC.BUFFALO.EDU.

 Following are the instructions for using FTP to copy DECNEWS files. If
 you've never used an FTP application, please consult with your support
 organization.  Depending on the software you have on your system, the
 commands may vary slightly:

 1. Use the INTERNET application, FTP, to connect to gatekeeper.dec.com.
    (16.1.0.2 is the address if you don't have it defined)

 2. Login as user: anonymous

 3. Enter a password.  You may use any string as the password, but we
    prefer that you use your e-mail address.

 4. Change to the DECNEWS directory; for example:
    cd pub/DEC/DECinfo/DECnews-EDU

 5. Use the get command to get the file; for example: get news0201.txt

 Note that the username in step 2, the directory in step 4, and the
 filename in step 5 are case sensitive; they must be typed as shown.
 Also, ".txt" must be used instead of " txt" (space txt).

